# This repo is developed on Windows with core.autocrlf=true, so tracked files
# are checked out with CRLF by default. That is fine for sources the toolchain
# reads, but fatal for a shell script the MSYS/Git-bash `bash` actually
# executes: every trailing \r ends up inside the token it terminates, so
# `TIMEOUT="${TIMEOUT:-300}"` yields "300\r" and the first arithmetic
# comparison against it fails.
#
# The Hibernate suite runner and its per-class override table are tracked
# specifically so they cannot silently vanish (see
# apps/hib-suite-runner/class-overrides.tsv's header). Pin them to LF so the
# copy git materialises is the copy that runs.
#
# Pinned for EVERY tracked shell script, not just the two noticed first. The
# hazard is a property of "git materialises this file and bash executes it", so
# an allow-list of individual paths only waits for the next script to be added
# — `probes/*.sh`, including the pre-existing hib-mapresize reproducer, was
# already exposed while this file listed just the two below.
*.sh text eol=lf
apps/hib-suite-runner/run-hib.sh text eol=lf
apps/hib-suite-runner/class-overrides.tsv text eol=lf
apps/hib-suite-runner/known-benign-aborts.tsv text eol=lf
